Retain the supplied GRU backbone and shifted next-item targets. At each valid position, score the positive and K=64 sampled negatives with the same item_emb. For positive scores p shaped [N] and negative scores n shaped [N,K], implement:

def bpr_max(p, n, reg=0.1):
    w = torch.softmax(n, dim=-1)
    log_win = torch.logsumexp(torch.log_softmax(n, dim=-1) + torch.nn.functional.logsigmoid(p[:, None] - n), dim=-1)
    return (-log_win + reg * (w * n.square()).sum(-1)).mean()

Exclude padding, positive collisions and training-history items from negatives; use bounded sampling for users with few eligible items. Initial settings: hidden=128, one GRU layer, dropout=0.1, Adam lr=0.001, reg=0.1. Shared contract for all four directions: DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR']; preserve all four categories, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, supplied splits, 200 batches/epoch and at most 200 epochs. Train and retain exactly one model/checkpoint per category, without score fusion. Write artifacts beneath the trial directory. Preserve sample_batch and ModelView compatibility through log2feats(sequence), item_emb and predict_score(features, items). Use the final nonpadding index for LEFT-padded readout. Update checkpoint metadata and the predictor writer whenever architecture or scoring changes; select using pinned validation macro HR@10 only.
